  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "ServiceNow sys_audit / sys_security_audit_history → AKSI control ID mapping. ServiceNow is the dominant ITSM platform and Now Assist (their AI agent surface) creates incidents, transitions change requests, drafts/publishes knowledge articles, and qualifies records. The ``reason`` column distinguishes web/api/workflow/now_assist/automation/system; ``is_now_assist`` and ``now_assist_capability`` identify AI-attributed mutations. Tables: incident, change_request, problem, sc_request, kb_knowledge, task, sys_user, sys_user_role, sys_security_acl. Now Assist creating an incident is a PR-01 FLAG (review). Now Assist transitioning an incident to Resolved/Closed is PR-02 FAIL (autonomous resolution). Change-request implementation by Now Assist with approval_state≠approved is PR-02 FAIL. Admin-role grants and ACL mutations are PR-02 FAIL. Now Assist editing a sensitive field is PR-04 FLAG. basic auth on production ServiceNow is PR-04 FAIL. workflow/automation reasons are PR-05 PASS. Synthetic findings: now-assist velocity (>50/h), cross-table (>5/h), and sensitive-field-burst (>20/h). All identifiers are stripped to last-8; old/new values are NEVER stored (length only). client_ip masked to /16. usernames are pseudonymous and stored verbatim.",
